  "worked_solution": "First, we calculate $P(A)$ using the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A\\cup B) & =P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ \\frac{5}{6} & =P(A)+\\frac{2}{5}-\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ P(A) & =\\frac{5}{6}+\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{2}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{30}+\\frac{10}{30}-\\frac{12}{30} \\\\  & =\\frac{23}{30}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we construct the corresponding Venn diagram and shade the region ${A}^{\u2032}\\cup {B}^{\u2032}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/assets/4b5f335b449e5f07de1d9ac1590245e71f6825b2dc13fe4ba046985aac95465a.png)\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P({A}^{\u2032}\\cup {B}^{\u2032}) & =\\frac{13}{30}+\\frac{1}{15}+\\frac{1}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{13}{30}+\\frac{2}{30}+\\frac{5}{30} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
